## Why This Is Asked
Tests practical CKNE-to-quotas mapping, token-based fairness, and SLA guarantees in a real-world multi-tenant dispatch scenario.

## Key Concepts
- CKNE-to-quotas mapping
- Token-bucket with a global minute cap
- Minute-by-minute reallocation and carryover
- SLA baseline with priority to high-CKNE tenants

## Code Example
```javascript
function allocateQuotas(totalCap, tenants) {
  const sumCKNE = tenants.reduce((s,t)=>s+t.ckne,0) || 1;
  return tenants.map(t => {
    const q = Math.floor(totalCap * (t.ckne / sumCKNE));
    return {tenant: t.tenant, quota: Math.max(1, q)};
  });
}
```

## Follow-up Questions
- How would you handle new tenants joining or CKNE updates during a minute?
- What telemetry would you collect to verify fairness and SLA adherence?

## Why This Is Asked
Prompts candidates to design CKNE-driven admission control and fairness in real-time multi-tenant streams, a practical production concern.

## Key Concepts
- CKNE signals to compute per-tenant health
- Dynamic rate limiting and cross-tenant shedding
- Payload schema for health metadata and token updates
- Minute-level control loop with smoothing

## Code Example

```javascript
function healthScore(p95Latency, errRate, queueDepth){
  const normLat = Math.min(p95Latency / 1000, 1);
  const normErr = Math.min(errRate, 1);
  const normQ = Math.min(queueDepth / 1000, 1);
  // Weighted mix: latency matters more
  return 0.55 * normLat + 0.25 * normErr + 0.20 * normQ;
}
```

